# Map hover = two facts

The hover answers one question in about a second: **what is that dot?**

Maximum two facts. Never a miniature Decision Card. Never the title (title belongs to click/popup).

1. **Value** (always, when we have one)
2. **One horizon-specific reason to care**
   - Open → agency (`$208K` / `Army`)
   - Recompete → time to expiration (`$1.2M` / `Expires in 18 days`) — relative only, no calendar date
   - Forecast → expected buying period (`$50M` / `Expected Q2 FY26`) — no "in", no ~months

Ladder: Dot → exists. Hover → value + one reason. Click/Decision Card → title, agency, location, DNA, deadline. Listing → everything.

If the preferred second fact is missing, fall back to agency. Never invent a date.
